 @shatteredsentient5321  sorry if I was ambiguous about what I meant. What I meant was, if you want to push over 100fps, then you ought to optimise your settings - do away with any setting that saps performance and offers little visual fidelity gains. 

For instance, I like to have The Witcher III: Wild Hunt sitting at around 130-144fps. If I turn on Nvidia hair works (or whatever it's called), my fps tanks massively. 

It's not that there's some kind of relation between "ultra" settings and refresh rate. I wouldn't recommend buying a 60hz monitor.

 @WastdTrashPanda  
now add Reshade and other graphical Mods and the 3060ti starts to suffer at 1440p. Reshade alone (Clarity + Colorfulness + Luma Sharpen + (fake) HDR) eats between 8 and 15fps. then add 4K Texture Mods and such and you will see the difference.
Not to mention Raytracing or (fake) Raytracing Shaders via Reshade.

